 to push  directly on the corner of this little  box I have here so if I push here like  that these are now Valley folds okay and  what you're going to do is you're going  to lift the  corner up in between these two folds  here what you want to first do though is  you're going to push on that little line  there so you want to push on that line  and you're going to pinch these two  folds together just like that  and now what you're going to do is  you're going to lift up this corner in  between these two folds so going to lift  up this corner in between those two  folds just like that okay and then just  give it a good crease and then you're  going to do the same with the left side  now they're directly opposite so as  you'll notice you can't really push  there if it's not open so what you do is  you're just going to push outwards on it  like this and then all you need to do is  to poke or push on the corner of this  little box there you might need to just  unfold some parts of it if it gets a  little wrinkled so it should look like  this and then you're going to push right  in the corner and you're going to  squeeze these two edges together now  make sure that these are valley folds in  the corner and then what you need to do  is you just need to lift up this corner  in between those two folds like that  and then just flatten flatten it out  like that and you should have something  that looks like this okay so what we're  going to do now is we're going to take  this little tip here and we're going to  fold it down so that it is flush with  the rest of the triangle here so just  fold it down like this until it's flush  with the rest of the triangle just like  that then you can unfold it and then  we're going to take the tip and we're  going to fold it directly onto that line  onto that fold that we just made so just  take the tip and fold it down like that  and then you can just crease it really  good also and then you could unfold that  part too now we're going to do is we're  going to pick up the model and as you'll  see this is where we tucked in this  corner here and this is where we tucked  in that corner we're going to do the  same with this corner and this corner  now so just hold it like this and you  want to take these two mountain folds  now the ones that are sticking up and  you're going to squeeze these two  together and now you should be able to  lift this corner up in between those two  so just pinch these two together like  that and this is kind of forming what  looks like an X here so just pinch these  two together now lift this up and then  just give it a nice crease then these  two you can also pinch together like  that and then you could lift up this  corner in between those two creases  so when you're done you should have  something that looks like this so what  we're going to do now is we're going to  flatten the model out and we're also  going to flatten these little mountain  folds out when we do that we want to  give them a counterclockwise spin so  this mountain fold is going to go up  this mountain fold is going to go to the  left this one's going to go down and  this one is going to go to the right so  what you need to do is just give this  little X in the middle a  counterclockwise spin like that and then  gently push down on everything so you'll  see here this fold should be down this  one should be to the right this one  should be up and this one should be to  the left just like that and when you do  that this X should sort of stick up in  the middle and what you're going to do  now is you're going to flatten this out  to do that we're going to pull on two  opposite parts of the X gently so just  gently push down on it like this and  then do the same with the other two and  it will sort of inflate or bubble up and  then what you can do is just gently push  down on it until it flattens out and  turns into a square so just push on that  it doesn't matter if it's a little  wrinkled it's not going to make a big  difference in the end but try to get it  as neat as possible and flatten it out  so it should look something like this so  this is known as the rose base and now  you have these flaps flattened out  remember they're going in a  counterclockwise direction and when you  flip it you'll also notice you have four  flaps here as well thanks for watching  part 1 of my tutorial for the origami  rose I hope you found it helpful now you  able to complete the row space to get to  part two all you need to do is to either  click the link on my hand or click one  of the links in the video description or  series playlist above before you go  don't forget to leave me a comment below  any questions feedback or video  responses post them below and I'll be  sure to take a look at them also if you  enjoy the video give me a thumbs up by  clicking the like button down to the  left and if you want to follow my videos  or subscribe for further notification  all you need to do is to click the  subscribe or follow button above

